1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,540
This is the implementation demo for journey fourteen,

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:05,740
the last of the buyer's journeys.

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:09,680
It is the real application and API running on this machine,

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:14,750
with synthetic people and the local adapters, so nothing is charged or sent.

5
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:18,550
It shows a buyer revisiting what they have had inspected.

6
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,700
This buyer has four inspections.

7
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:26,560
The Active tab holds the two that are not finished with: one booked for later,

8
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:30,730
and one whose call is done while the report is still being written.

9
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:35,600
The Past tab holds a completed inspection, with its estimate right on the row,

10
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,150
required repairs and what they cost, and a cancelled one.

11
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,950
Opening the completed row goes to its report.

12
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:46,320
Going back returns to the Past tab, because the tab is in the address.

13
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:50,930
Opening the cancelled row shows the car and the refund it was booked with,

14
00:00:50,930 --> 00:00:53,420
so history never changes after the fact.

15
00:00:54,570 --> 00:00:57,650
Now a buyer with forty-five past inspections.

16
00:00:57,650 --> 00:01:01,540
The list shows twenty to a page, says how many there are,

17
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:03,870
and says which rows are on screen.

18
00:01:03,870 --> 00:01:06,540
Previous is disabled on the first page.

19
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:10,640
Next moves on, and the last page shows the five that remain,

20
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:13,510
with Next disabled and Previous available.

21
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:19,560
A buyer with no inspections sees how to start, and can open a sample report,

22
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,240
clearly marked as made up.

23
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:26,660
Back on the buyer with four inspections, a list that fails to load says it is on our

24
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:32,010
side, that the bookings are safe, and offers Try again or a way to contact support.

25
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:36,980
Trying again shows the list busy with placeholder rows, then the inspections.

26
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:40,640
The rules are enforced by the server.

27
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:44,240
The tabs and their counts come from the same request.

28
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:49,600
A page past the end is empty, a different buyer sees none of these inspections,

29
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,640
and an unknown tab is refused.

30
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:55,650
The mechanic is refused, and so is a request with no token.

31
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,520
Here is what to remember.

32
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:03,900
Active holds what is not finished with, and Past holds completed and cancelled

33
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,180
inspections with their estimates.

34
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:11,560
Pages keep a long history manageable, and the tab and page are in the address.

35
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,660
A buyer only ever sees their own inspections.

36
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:16,590
That completes the journeys.

37
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:21,830
Not built yet: make, model and location on each row, and a retention policy.
